(-: A Suno song from {teacher}'s words (-:

    ( What is given (
        The quotations given follow this prompt, each with its id, its source
        and its verification status. The style chosen follows them, from the
        Suno lens of the Smile library.
    ) End what is given ) thank you

    ( What to write (
        A song for Suno on {topic}, made from {teacher}'s words.
        The lyrics are at most {lyrics_max} characters, counting every tag,
        space and line break. The style is at most {style_max} characters.
        Sung lines are taken from the quotations verbatim, or cut down with
        an ellipsis. Lines you add so the song can sing are yours, and are
        few.
        The tags follow the Suno lens, each on its own line in square
        brackets, naming the voice, the part and the sound, e.g. [Woman],
        [Chorus of women Sing together], [Male deep], [Said kindly],
        [Bass drop], [Music stays loud], and an instruction tag such as
        [ALL LYRICS MUST BE SAID CORRECTLY AT ALL TIMES] where the words
        must be heard whole.
        The style starts from the chosen style and turns it toward the
        song's mood, in Suno's comma separated tags.
    ) End what to write ) Many blessings

    [= The reply [=
        STYLE on a line of its own, then the style.
        LYRICS on a line of its own, then the lyrics.
        SOURCES on a line of its own, then each sung line's quotation id,
        and every line that is yours marked as yours.
        COUNT on a line of its own, then the lyrics' character count.
    =] End the reply =] Warm thanks

:-) End a Suno song from {teacher}'s words :-) So much gratitude
